In its application to the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (hereinafter referred to as the "Organization"), the standard provisions shall be in force with the following exceptions:

1. Article V and paragraph 2 (I) of Article VII shall also apply to the President of the Council of the Organization, except that any waiver of the immunity of the President under paragraph 16 shall be made by the Council of the Organization.

2. (i) Experts (other than officials covered by Article VI) serving as members of committees or as staff of the Organization shall be accorded the following privileges and immunities to the extent necessary for the independent exercise of their functions, including the time spent in travelling in connection with the exercise of their functions in those committees or in the performance of their duties:

(a) immunity from personal arrest or detention and from search, provided that the immunity from immunity from personal arrest or detention and from search shall not apply to crimes committed against the life, physical integrity or health of others;

(b) immunity from legal process in respect of words spoken or written and acts done by them in their official capacity; this immunity shall continue to be accorded after they have ceased to hold office in the committees of the Organization or to perform their duties for the Organization;

(c) the same facilities as regards restrictions on the movement and use of funds and the exchange of currency.

